### ION package build output
# packages/*/src is the source; everything below is produced by
# `node scripts/build-packages.mjs` and must never be committed — a stale
# committed bundle silently shadowing a rebuilt one is the exact failure this
# avoids.
packages/*/dist/
packages/editor/studio/
packages/build/lib/
# Hashes of the built payload — regenerated by the same build.
packages/*/ion-integrity.json
.visual-regression/

### Synced dev-server copies
# scripts/sync-assets.js (npm's `predev`) mirrors tools/ui-editor.html into
# public/ so Vite serves it at /ui-editor.html. tools/ is the source; the copy
# was committed byte-identical, which is pure diff noise and a real drift risk
# — an edit to the wrong file looks like it works right up until the next sync
# silently reverts it.
public/ui-editor.html
